From 4b2811efb1ae66065568c3746e3116963f0d8c98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 05:06:29 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] metal: tune routed vector reuse and bounded offsets

Retain the qualified output-row reuse specializations. Add checked uint32
relative offsets for qualified shared-buffer R4 and R8 geometries. Enable R8
by default on M1 Ultra and M5 Max, and R4 on M1 Ultra. Keep other devices on
the original default and preserve private diagnostic overrides.

Share the existing quantized-vector arithmetic between both offset widths.
Preserve unsupported-shape, stride, byte-span and old-library fallbacks, with
cached positive and negative function discovery. Add CPU-only policy CTest
coverage and explicit native paired/FP64/masked/view/fallback qualification.
The public Skippy ABI and stored model bytes remain unchanged.
